---
title: Ask before a tool runs
id: ui-recipe-tool-approval
order: 3
description: "Gate a tool behind a yes or no. Render the approval next to the tool, or in a list."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - tool approval
  - needsApproval
  - interruptsComponents
  - example
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to the tool. The run pauses and your UI gets an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" prop."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'deleteFile',\n  description: 'Delete a file',\n  needsApproval: true,\n  inputSchema: z.object({ path: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ deleted: z.boolean() }),\n}).client()","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You choose where the approval appears. Two places are available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-to-the-tool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next to the tool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tool component receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part"},{"type":"text","value":". Render the buttons there."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'deleteFile',\n  description: 'Delete a file',\n  needsApproval: true,\n  inputSchema: z.object({ path: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ deleted: z.boolean() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [deleteFile],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages }) => <main><Messages /></main>,\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    text: ({ part }) => <p>{part.content}</p>,\n    fallback: () => null,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    deleteFile: ({ part, interrupt }) => {\n      if (interrupt?.status === 'pending') {\n        return (\n          <div>\n            <p>Delete {part.input?.path}?</p>\n            <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)}>\n              Delete\n            </button>\n            <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(false)}>\n              Keep\n            </button>\n          </div>\n        )\n      }\n      if (part.state === 'complete') {\n        return <p>{part.output?.deleted ? 'Deleted' : 'Kept'}</p>\n      }\n      return <p>{part.input?.path}</p>\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function FileChat() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=inline-approval"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt(true)"},{"type":"text","value":" approves. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt(false)"},{"type":"text","value":" denies. The run continues either way."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"in-a-list-instead","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In a list instead"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some apps collect every pending decision in one place. Register the tool name under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" and the approval moves out of the message."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { InterruptProps } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\n\nexport function DeleteApproval({\n  interrupt,\n}: InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'deleteFile'>) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Delete {interrupt.originalArgs.path}?</p>\n      <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)}>Delete</button>\n      <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(false)}>Keep</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=inline-approval"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then wire it up and render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":" in the layout:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages, Interrupts }) => (\n      <main>\n        <Messages />\n        <Interrupts />\n      </main>\n    ),\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    deleteFile: ({ part }) => <p>{part.input?.path}</p>,\n  },\n  interruptsComponents: {\n    tools: { deleteFile: DeleteApproval },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tool component no longer reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":". Its approval is in the list."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pick-one-place-per-tool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick one place per tool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register the tool under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" and the approval renders in the list. Leave it out and the approval reaches the tool component instead. Do not do both for one tool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.originalArgs"},{"type":"text","value":" holds the arguments the model proposed. It is typed from the tool's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" is a string here."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A decision that is not about a tool? See "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-interrupt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a custom interrupt"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More on the protocol behind this: "},{"type":"link","href":"../../interrupts/tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool approval"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"next-to-the-tool","text":"Next to the tool","level":2},{"id":"in-a-list-instead","text":"In a list instead","level":2},{"id":"pick-one-place-per-tool","text":"Pick one place per tool","level":2},{"id":"next","text":"Next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nAdd `needsApproval: true` to the tool. The run pauses and your UI gets an `interrupt` prop.\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'deleteFile',\n  description: 'Delete a file',\n  needsApproval: true,\n  inputSchema: z.object({ path: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ deleted: z.boolean() }),\n}).client()\n```\n\nYou choose where the approval appears. Two places are available.\n\n## Next to the tool\n\nThe tool component receives `interrupt` alongside `part`. Render the buttons there.\n\n```tsx group=inline-approval\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'deleteFile',\n  description: 'Delete a file',\n  needsApproval: true,\n  inputSchema: z.object({ path: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ deleted: z.boolean() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [deleteFile],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages }) => <main><Messages /></main>,\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    text: ({ part }) => <p>{part.content}</p>,\n    fallback: () => null,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    deleteFile: ({ part, interrupt }) => {\n      if (interrupt?.status === 'pending') {\n        return (\n          <div>\n            <p>Delete {part.input?.path}?</p>\n            <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)}>\n              Delete\n            </button>\n            <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(false)}>\n              Keep\n            </button>\n          </div>\n        )\n      }\n      if (part.state === 'complete') {\n        return <p>{part.output?.deleted ? 'Deleted' : 'Kept'}</p>\n      }\n      return <p>{part.input?.path}</p>\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function FileChat() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\n`resolveInterrupt(true)` approves. `resolveInterrupt(false)` denies. The run continues either way.\n\n## In a list instead\n\nSome apps collect every pending decision in one place. Register the tool name under `interruptsComponents.tools` and the approval moves out of the message.\n\n```tsx group=inline-approval\nimport type { InterruptProps } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\n\nexport function DeleteApproval({\n  interrupt,\n}: InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'deleteFile'>) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Delete {interrupt.originalArgs.path}?</p>\n      <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)}>Delete</button>\n      <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(false)}>Keep</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThen wire it up and render `Interrupts` in the layout:\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages, Interrupts }) => (\n      <main>\n        <Messages />\n        <Interrupts />\n      </main>\n    ),\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    deleteFile: ({ part }) => <p>{part.input?.path}</p>,\n  },\n  interruptsComponents: {\n    tools: { deleteFile: DeleteApproval },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe tool component no longer reads `interrupt`. Its approval is in the list.\n\n## Pick one place per tool\n\nRegister the tool under `interruptsComponents.tools` and the approval renders in the list. Leave it out and the approval reaches the tool component instead. Do not do both for one tool.\n\n`interrupt.originalArgs` holds the arguments the model proposed. It is typed from the tool's `inputSchema`, so `path` is a string here.\n\n## Next\n\n- A decision that is not about a tool? See [a custom interrupt](./custom-interrupt).\n- More on the protocol behind this: [tool approval](../../interrupts/tool-approval).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Ask before a tool runs\nid: ui-recipe-tool-approval\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Gate a tool behind a yes or no. Render the approval next to the tool, or in a list.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - tool approval\n  - needsApproval\n  - interruptsComponents\n  - example\n---\n\nAdd `needsApproval: true` to the tool. The run pauses and your UI gets an `interrupt` prop.\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'deleteFile',\n  description: 'Delete a file',\n  needsApproval: true,\n  inputSchema: z.object({ path: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ deleted: z.boolean() }),\n}).client()\n```\n\nYou choose where the approval appears. Two places are available.\n\n## Next to the tool\n\nThe tool component receives `interrupt` alongside `part`. Render the buttons there.\n\n```tsx group=inline-approval\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'deleteFile',\n  description: 'Delete a file',\n  needsApproval: true,\n  inputSchema: z.object({ path: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ deleted: z.boolean() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [deleteFile],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages }) => <main><Messages /></main>,\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    text: ({ part }) => <p>{part.content}</p>,\n    fallback: () => null,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    deleteFile: ({ part, interrupt }) => {\n      if (interrupt?.status === 'pending') {\n        return (\n          <div>\n            <p>Delete {part.input?.path}?</p>\n            <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)}>\n              Delete\n            </button>\n            <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(false)}>\n              Keep\n            </button>\n          </div>\n        )\n      }\n      if (part.state === 'complete') {\n        return <p>{part.output?.deleted ? 'Deleted' : 'Kept'}</p>\n      }\n      return <p>{part.input?.path}</p>\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function FileChat() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\n`resolveInterrupt(true)` approves. `resolveInterrupt(false)` denies. The run continues either way.\n\n## In a list instead\n\nSome apps collect every pending decision in one place. Register the tool name under `interruptsComponents.tools` and the approval moves out of the message.\n\n```tsx group=inline-approval\nimport type { InterruptProps } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\n\nexport function DeleteApproval({\n  interrupt,\n}: InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'deleteFile'>) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Delete {interrupt.originalArgs.path}?</p>\n      <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)}>Delete</button>\n      <button onClick={() => interrupt.resolveInterrupt(false)}>Keep</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThen wire it up and render `Interrupts` in the layout:\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages, Interrupts }) => (\n      <main>\n        <Messages />\n        <Interrupts />\n      </main>\n    ),\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: () => null },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    deleteFile: ({ part }) => <p>{part.input?.path}</p>,\n  },\n  interruptsComponents: {\n    tools: { deleteFile: DeleteApproval },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe tool component no longer reads `interrupt`. Its approval is in the list.\n\n## Pick one place per tool\n\nRegister the tool under `interruptsComponents.tools` and the approval renders in the list. Leave it out and the approval reaches the tool component instead. Do not do both for one tool.\n\n`interrupt.originalArgs` holds the arguments the model proposed. It is typed from the tool's `inputSchema`, so `path` is a string here.\n\n## Next\n\n- A decision that is not about a tool? See [a custom interrupt](./custom-interrupt).\n- More on the protocol behind this: [tool approval](../../interrupts/tool-approval).\n"}
